WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.640
Many Muslim women cover their
hair as a duty from God,

2
00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:05.720
held by most scholars.

3
00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:10.430
Others have called the veil a barrier,
holding women back from education and public

4
00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:11.500
life.

5
00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:15.310
Yet the Qur'an's call to
modesty speaks first to men:

6
00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:18.390
lower your gaze and guard your modesty.

7
00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:24.320
Oppression, faith, protest: so
how can one cloth mean all three?

8
00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:27.120
In this mission, you'll
read the verses on modesty,

9
00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:30.270
and sort out words like hijab and niqab.

10
00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:34.660
Then you'll weigh up one claim that
divides Muslims and non-Muslims alike:

11
00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:37.470
the veil is a symbol of oppression.

12
00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:42.240
Your mission: find out how one piece of
cloth can carry such different meanings

13
00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:43.310
for Muslim women.
